2026-07-28T06:37:17.0822728Z [36;1m# standard flags R selects per version (e.g. -std=gnu2x for C, -std=gnu++17[0m
2026-07-28T06:37:17.0823240Z [36;1m# / -std=gnu++20 for C++); a plain "CC = ccache gcc" override would drop[0m
2026-07-28T06:37:17.0823728Z [36;1m# them and silently downgrade the standard across the version matrix.[0m
2026-07-28T06:37:17.0824217Z [36;1m# Inference uses an empty user Makevars so we always read the pristine[0m
2026-07-28T06:37:17.0824649Z [36;1m# Makeconf defaults, never a value we just wrote.[0m
2026-07-28T06:37:17.0825532Z [36;1m# Note: the versioned switches (CXX11..CXX23) intentionally come out as[0m
2026-07-28T06:37:17.0826025Z [36;1m# bare "g++" with no -std flag. R keeps the standard in a separate[0m
